Chapter: ProbeClosureLetformSolo

 Separates the driver SHAPE from the chapter CONTENTS. This is
 probe-closure-letform with relay-once removed, so the chapter is exactly
 probe-closure-solo's and only the driver differs.

 probe-closure-solo   chain driver, no relay-once  -> 47
 probe-closure-letform  let driver, relay-once      -> 6291472
 this probe           let driver, no relay-once     -> ?

 47 here means the chapter contents matter: relay-once's presence is what
 breaks the let form. A heap address here means the let form is broken on
 its own, relay-once is irrelevant, and solo's 47 came from the chain
 form rather than from the chapter being clean.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let f = make-adder 5
    in print-line-uni ("letform-solo " & show ((f 20) 22))
  end
